---
import SimLayout from '../../../layouts/SimLayout.astro';
---

<SimLayout
  areaSlug="generative-ai"
  title="Autoregressive Models"
  description="One loop, repeated forever: give every word in the vocabulary a probability, cut the unlikely tail, pick one, append it. The vocabulary here is 40 words instead of 100,000, so you can watch temperature, top-k and top-p act on all of it at once."
>
  <div class="sim" id="wrap">
    <div class="sim-stage">
      <canvas id="ar" width="1000" height="936"></canvas>
    </div>

    <div class="sim-panel">
      <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap">
        <button class="btn" id="run">Run</button>
        <button class="btn ghost" id="step">Next word</button>
        <button class="btn ghost" id="reset">Restart</button>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <div class="seg" id="mode">
          <button data-m="sample" class="active">Sampling</button>
          <button data-m="greedy">Greedy</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="control tunes">
        <label>Temperature <b id="tval">0.80</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="t" min="5" max="200" value="80" />
      </div>

      <div class="control tunes">
        <label>Top-k <b id="kval">off</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="k" min="1" max="40" value="40" />
      </div>

      <div class="control tunes">
        <label>Top-p <b id="pval">off</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="p" min="5" max="100" value="100" />
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Context length (words) <b id="nval">2</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="n" min="1" max="3" value="2" />
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Speed <b id="spval">3</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="sp" min="1" max="16" value="3" />
      </div>

      <div class="readout">
        <div class="row"><span>Vocabulary</span><b id="vocab">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span>Seen after this context</span><b id="seen">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span>Kept by the cut</span><b id="kept">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span>Mass kept</span><b id="mass">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span>Last pick</span><b id="pick">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span>Surprise of that pick</span><b id="bits">—</b></div>
      </div>

      <p style="font-size:.82rem;color:var(--text-faint);margin:0;line-height:1.5">
        Every word of the vocabulary gets a probability at every step, never
        zero, exactly as in a real model. Top-k and top-p decide how much of
        that tail is allowed to win.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Fragment slot="observe">
    <li>
      Look at the vocabulary map at the bottom: <b>every one of the 40 words has
      a bar at every step</b>, even the absurd ones. Words the model has seen
      after this context get most of the probability, the rest get a sliver.
      That sliver is the whole reason top-k and top-p exist.
    </li>
    <li>
      Set <b>top-k</b> to 1. That is greedy: the tallest bar wins every time,
      nothing is random, and the text falls into a loop. Slide it back up and
      the loop breaks.
    </li>
    <li>
      Leave both cuts off and run. The dart can land anywhere, so sooner or
      later a word from the sliver tail wins and the sentence derails. Any one
      of them is unlikely, but there are 35 of them.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>Top-k</b> keeps a fixed count. When the model is certain, k = 10 drags
      in nine words it did not believe in; when it is genuinely torn, the same
      k = 10 may cut off good ones. The count is fixed, the confidence is not.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>Top-p</b> instead keeps the fewest words whose probabilities already
      add up to p. Watch "kept by the cut" as you step: it shrinks to 1 or 2
      where the model is sure and swells where it hesitates. Holding the mass
      fixed is what makes the cut adapt.
    </li>
    <li>
      Drag <b>temperature</b> without stepping. The pale bars, the model's own
      probabilities, never move; the solid bars do. Near 0 everything collapses
      onto the top word, high up they flatten toward uniform. The same numbers,
      only reshaped before the cut.
    </li>
    <li>
      The strip is where sampling becomes concrete: the surviving words laid end
      to end from 0 to 1, each as wide as its probability, and a random number
      thrown at it. Wide segments win often, slivers win rarely, and that is all
      "sampling from a distribution" means.
    </li>
    <li>
      Raise <b>context length</b>. With one word the text wanders; with three it
      can only replay phrases it has seen. Fluent and unoriginal, or original
      and unhinged, is the trade every language model lives on.
    </li>
  </Fragment>
</SimLayout>

<script>
  import { setupCanvas } from '../../../lib/sim';
  import { equationBar } from '../../../lib/equation';

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // The next-token loop, one panel per stage: the text so far, a probability for
  // every word in the vocabulary, the cut that throws the tail away, the dart
  // that picks one. Counts stand in for a neural network, and a small smoothing
  // term stands in for the softmax: no word is ever exactly impossible.
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  const CORPUS = `the cat sleeps in the sun . the dog runs in the rain . the cat
    runs to the door . the dog sleeps by the fire . the girl opens the door and
    the cat runs out . the boy feeds the dog by the fire . the rain falls on the
    roof . the sun warms the roof . the cat watches the rain from the window .
    the dog watches the door . the girl calls the dog and the dog runs to the
    girl . the boy calls the cat and the cat sleeps . the night falls and the
    house grows quiet . the cat sleeps by the fire and the dog sleeps by the
    door . in the morning the sun returns and the girl opens the window . the
    boy runs out to the garden . the dog follows the boy . the cat watches from
    the roof . the rain returns in the evening . the house grows warm and the
    fire burns . the girl reads by the window . the boy sleeps . the cat and the
    dog sleep by the fire .`;

  const TOKENS = (CORPUS.toLowerCase().match(/[a-z]+|\./g) || []);
  const VOCAB = [...new Set(TOKENS)].sort((a, b) => {
    const pa = a === '.' ? 1 : 0, pb = b === '.' ? 1 : 0;
    return pa - pb || a.localeCompare(b);
  });
  const V = VOCAB.length;

  /**
   * Every word gets `ALPHA` of a count for free, so the distribution covers the
   * whole vocabulary. Without it an n-gram says "impossible" to most words,
   * which a real model never does, and there would be no tail for top-k and
   * top-p to cut.
   */
  const ALPHA = 0.02;

  const state = {
    greedy: false,
    n: 2,
    temp: 0.8,
    k: V,
    p: 1,
    speed: 3,
    running: false,
  };

  // --- the model --------------------------------------------------------------

  let models: Map<string, Map<string, number>>[] = [];
  let tokens: string[] = [];

  function buildModels() {
    models = [];
    for (let order = 1; order <= 3; order++) {
      const m = new Map<string, Map<string, number>>();
      for (let i = order; i < TOKENS.length; i++) {
        const k = TOKENS.slice(i - order, i).join(' ');
        if (!m.has(k)) m.set(k, new Map());
        const inner = m.get(k)!;
        inner.set(TOKENS[i], (inner.get(TOKENS[i]) || 0) + 1);
      }
      models[order] = m;
    }
  }

  /** The longest slice of recent words the corpus has actually seen. */
  function usedContext(): string[] {
    for (let order = Math.min(state.n, tokens.length); order >= 1; order--) {
      const ctxTok = tokens.slice(-order);
      const m = models[order].get(ctxTok.join(' '));
      if (m && m.size) return ctxTok;
    }
    return [];
  }

  function counts(): Map<string, number> {
    const c = usedContext();
    if (c.length) return models[c.length].get(c.join(' '))!;
    const uni = new Map<string, number>();
    for (const t of TOKENS) uni.set(t, (uni.get(t) || 0) + 1);
    return uni;
  }

  type Cand = {
    w: string;
    /** how often it followed this context in the text */
    n: number;
    /** the model's own probability, smoothing included */
    base: number;
    /** after temperature, before anything is cut */
    q: number;
    /** what the dart actually sees: 0 for a word that was cut */
    final: number;
    kept: boolean;
    cum: number;
  };

  function candidates(): Cand[] {
    const c = counts();
    let N = 0;
    c.forEach((v) => (N += v));
    const denom = N + ALPHA * V;
    const inv = 1 / Math.max(0.05, state.temp);

    const arr: Cand[] = [];
    let z = 0;
    for (const w of VOCAB) {
      const n = c.get(w) || 0;
      const base = (n + ALPHA) / denom;
      const q = Math.pow(base, inv);
      z += q;
      arr.push({ w, n, base, q, final: 0, kept: false, cum: 0 });
    }
    for (const a of arr) a.q /= z || 1;
    arr.sort((a, b) => b.q - a.q || a.w.localeCompare(b.w));

    // top-k first, then top-p inside what survives, the order real samplers use
    let keep = Math.min(arr.length, state.k);
    if (state.p < 1) {
      let acc = 0;
      for (let i = 0; i < keep; i++) {
        acc += arr[i].q;
        if (acc >= state.p - 1e-12) { keep = i + 1; break; }
      }
    }
    if (state.greedy) keep = 1;

    let kz = 0;
    for (let i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
      arr[i].kept = i < keep;
      if (arr[i].kept) kz += arr[i].q;
    }
    let cum = 0;
    for (const a of arr) {
      a.final = a.kept ? a.q / (kz || 1) : 0;
      cum += a.final;
      a.cum = cum;
    }
    return arr;
  }

  /** The last dart, kept on screen so the pick can be looked at afterwards. */
  type Shot = {
    ctxStr: string;
    kept: { w: string; p: number }[];
    r: number;
    word: string;
    prob: number;
    base: number;
    cutCount: number;
  };
  let shot: Shot | null = null;
  let flash = 0;

  function contextString() {
    const used = usedContext();
    return (used.length ? used : tokens.slice(-state.n)).join(' ') || '(start)';
  }

  function seed() {
    tokens = ['the'];
    shot = null;
    flash = 0;
  }

  function stepOnce() {
    const cands = candidates();
    const kept = cands.filter((c) => c.kept);
    if (!kept.length) return;
    const r = Math.random();
    let chosen = kept[0];
    if (!state.greedy) {
      let acc = 0;
      chosen = kept[kept.length - 1];
      for (const c of kept) {
        acc += c.final;
        if (r <= acc) { chosen = c; break; }
      }
    }
    shot = {
      ctxStr: contextString(),
      kept: kept.map((c) => ({ w: c.w, p: c.final })),
      r: state.greedy ? -1 : r,
      word: chosen.w,
      prob: chosen.final,
      base: chosen.base,
      cutCount: cands.length - kept.length,
    };
    flash = 1;
    tokens.push(chosen.w);
    if (tokens.length > 150) tokens = tokens.slice(-130);
  }

  // --- canvas -----------------------------------------------------------------

  const canvas = document.getElementById('ar') as HTMLCanvasElement;
  const { ctx, W, H } = setupCanvas(canvas, () => draw());
  const cssVar = (n: string) => getComputedStyle(canvas).getPropertyValue(n).trim();
  const inkRGB = () => cssVar('--stage-ink') || '232,233,236';
  const inkA = (a: number) => `rgba(${inkRGB()},${a})`;

  const KEEP = '#7c8cff';   // survives the cut, and is sampled from
  const CHOSEN = '#34d399'; // the word that was actually written
  const DART = '#fbbf24';   // the random number
  const CUTC = '#f9736a';   // where the tail gets chopped off

  function hexA(hex: string, a: number) {
    const h = hex.replace('#', '');
    const s = h.length === 3 ? h.split('').map((c) => c + c).join('') : h;
    const n = parseInt(s, 16);
    return `rgba(${(n >> 16) & 255},${(n >> 8) & 255},${n & 255},${a})`;
  }

  const UI = (size: number, weight = 400) =>
    `${weight} ${size}px 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif`;
  const MONO = (size: number) => `${size}px 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace`;

  function text(
    s: string,
    x: number,
    y: number,
    size: number,
    col: string,
    align: CanvasTextAlign = 'left',
    mono = false,
    weight = 400
  ) {
    ctx.font = mono ? MONO(size) : UI(size, weight);
    ctx.fillStyle = col;
    ctx.textAlign = align;
    ctx.fillText(s, x, y);
    ctx.textAlign = 'left';
  }

  type Box = { x: number; y: number; w: number; h: number };
  function rr(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, r: number) {
    const rad = Math.min(r, Math.abs(w) / 2, Math.abs(h) / 2);
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(x + rad, y);
    ctx.lineTo(x + w - rad, y);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(x + w, y, x + w, y + rad);
    ctx.lineTo(x + w, y + h - rad);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(x + w, y + h, x + w - rad, y + h);
    ctx.lineTo(x + rad, y + h);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(x, y + h, x, y + h - rad);
    ctx.lineTo(x, y + rad);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(x, y, x + rad, y);
    ctx.closePath();
  }
  function panel(b: Box, title: string) {
    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.1);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    rr(b.x, b.y, b.w, b.h, 10);
    ctx.stroke();
    text(title, b.x + 2, b.y - 9, 11, inkA(0.5), 'left', true);
  }

  const TEXTP: Box = { x: 20, y: 32, w: 960, h: 148 };
  const DIST: Box = { x: 20, y: 214, w: 604, h: 326 };
  const SIDE: Box = { x: 644, y: 214, w: 336, h: 326 };
  const DARTP: Box = { x: 20, y: 574, w: 960, h: 96 };
  const VOC: Box = { x: 20, y: 704, w: 960, h: 212 };

  // --- 1. the text so far ------------------------------------------------------

  /** Sentence case, purely so the toy text reads like text. */
  function shown(i: number) {
    const t = tokens[i];
    return i === 0 || tokens[i - 1] === '.' ? t[0].toUpperCase() + t.slice(1) : t;
  }

  function layoutText(from: number, x0: number, maxW: number) {
    ctx.font = UI(16);
    const spaceW = ctx.measureText(' ').width;
    const out: { s: string; i: number; x: number; row: number; w: number }[] = [];
    let x = x0, row = 0;
    for (let i = from; i < tokens.length; i++) {
      const s = shown(i);
      const w = ctx.measureText(s).width;
      let sep = i > from && s !== '.' ? spaceW : 0;
      if (x + sep + w > x0 + maxW) { x = x0; row++; sep = 0; }
      out.push({ s, i, x: x + sep, row, w });
      x += sep + w;
    }
    return { out, rows: row + 1, endX: x, spaceW };
  }

  function drawText() {
    panel(TEXTP, 'THE TEXT SO FAR, AND THE CONTEXT THE MODEL READS');
    const x0 = TEXTP.x + 18, rowH = 25, maxW = TEXTP.w - 36;
    const maxRows = Math.floor((TEXTP.h - 50) / rowH);
    let from = 0;
    let lay = layoutText(from, x0, maxW);
    while (lay.rows > maxRows && from < tokens.length - 1) {
      from += 4;
      lay = layoutText(from, x0, maxW);
    }
    const y0 = TEXTP.y + 30;
    const ctxLen = Math.max(1, usedContext().length || state.n);
    const ctxStart = Math.max(0, tokens.length - ctxLen);

    for (const t of lay.out) {
      const y = y0 + t.row * rowH;
      const inCtx = t.i >= ctxStart;
      if (inCtx) {
        ctx.fillStyle = hexA(KEEP, 0.18);
        rr(t.x - 3, y - 3, t.w + 6, rowH - 5, 4);
        ctx.fill();
      }
      if (t.i === tokens.length - 1 && flash > 0) {
        ctx.fillStyle = hexA(CHOSEN, 0.3 * flash);
        rr(t.x - 3, y - 3, t.w + 6, rowH - 5, 4);
        ctx.fill();
      }
      text(t.s, t.x, y + 14, 16, inCtx ? inkA(1) : inkA(0.62));
    }
    const lastRow = lay.out.length ? lay.out[lay.out.length - 1].row : 0;
    ctx.fillStyle = CHOSEN;
    ctx.fillRect(lay.endX + lay.spaceW, y0 + lastRow * rowH + 2, 2, rowH - 8);

    text(
      'highlighted = the words being conditioned on',
      TEXTP.x + 18,
      TEXTP.y + TEXTP.h - 13,
      11,
      inkA(0.4),
      'left',
      true
    );
  }

  // --- 2. the distribution ------------------------------------------------------

  function cutReason(keptN: number) {
    if (state.greedy) return 'greedy keeps only the top word';
    const kCut = state.k <= keptN;
    if (kCut && state.p < 1) return `top-k = ${state.k} stops here, top-p ${state.p.toFixed(2)} would too`;
    if (kCut) return `top-k = ${state.k} stops here`;
    return `top-p = ${state.p.toFixed(2)}: these ${keptN} words already carry it`;
  }

  function drawDist(cands: Cand[]) {
    panel(DIST, 'A PROBABILITY FOR EVERY WORD, BEST FIRST');
    text(
      `P(next word | "${contextString()}")`,
      DIST.x + 16,
      DIST.y + 26,
      12,
      inkA(0.6),
      'left',
      true
    );

    const ROWS = 9;
    const shownRows = cands.slice(0, ROWS);
    const rest = cands.slice(ROWS);
    const keptN = cands.filter((c) => c.kept).length;

    const lx = DIST.x + 16, labelW = 92;
    const bx = lx + labelW + 12;
    const numW = 112, cumW = 56;
    const barMax = DIST.w - 32 - labelW - 12 - numW - cumW;
    let maxP = 0.02;
    for (const c of shownRows) maxP = Math.max(maxP, c.base, c.final);

    const rowH = 24, y0 = DIST.y + 46;
    shownRows.forEach((c, i) => {
      const y = y0 + i * rowH;
      text(c.w, lx + labelW, y + 13, 14, c.kept ? inkA(0.95) : inkA(0.38), 'right');
      ctx.fillStyle = inkA(0.14);
      ctx.fillRect(bx, y + 1, Math.max(1, (c.base / maxP) * barMax), 17);
      if (c.kept) {
        ctx.fillStyle = i === 0 ? KEEP : hexA(KEEP, 0.62);
        ctx.fillRect(bx, y + 4, Math.max(1, (c.final / maxP) * barMax), 11);
      }
      text(
        `${(c.base * 100).toFixed(1)}% → ${c.kept ? (c.final * 100).toFixed(1) + '%' : 'cut'}`,
        bx + barMax + numW - 8,
        y + 13,
        11,
        c.kept ? inkA(0.75) : inkA(0.3),
        'right',
        true
      );
      if (c.kept)
        text(`Σ ${(c.cum * 100).toFixed(0)}%`, DIST.x + DIST.w - 16, y + 13, 11, inkA(0.42), 'right', true);
    });

    if (keptN < cands.length && keptN <= shownRows.length) {
      const y = y0 + keptN * rowH - 3;
      ctx.strokeStyle = hexA(CUTC, 0.7);
      ctx.lineWidth = 1.2;
      ctx.setLineDash([5, 4]);
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(lx, y);
      ctx.lineTo(DIST.x + DIST.w - 16, y);
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.setLineDash([]);
      text(cutReason(keptN), lx + 4, y - 5, 10, hexA(CUTC, 0.85), 'left', true);
    }

    if (rest.length) {
      const restKept = rest.filter((c) => c.kept).length;
      const restMass = rest.reduce((s, c) => s + c.final, 0);
      text(
        restKept
          ? `+ ${rest.length} more words, ${restKept} still in play, worth ${(restMass * 100).toFixed(1)}%`
          : `+ ${rest.length} more words, all cut`,
        lx,
        y0 + shownRows.length * rowH + 16,
        11,
        inkA(0.42),
        'left',
        true
      );
    }

    text(
      'pale bar = the model\'s own probability · solid bar = after temperature and the cut',
      DIST.x + 16,
      DIST.y + DIST.h - 13,
      10,
      inkA(0.4),
      'left',
      true
    );
  }

  // --- 3. what the cut did --------------------------------------------------------

  function drawSide(cands: Cand[]) {
    panel(SIDE, 'WHAT THE CUT DID');
    const x0 = SIDE.x + 18, maxW = SIDE.w - 36;

    const keptN = cands.filter((c) => c.kept).length;
    const keptMass = cands.reduce((s, c) => s + (c.kept ? c.q : 0), 0);
    const headline = state.greedy
      ? 'Greedy: the top word, always'
      : keptN === cands.length
        ? 'Nothing is cut'
        : `${keptN} words survive, ${cands.length - keptN} are gone`;
    text(headline, x0, SIDE.y + 34, 16, state.greedy ? CHOSEN : KEEP, 'left', false, 600);
    text(
      state.greedy
        ? 'no dart, so the same context always gives the same word'
        : keptN === cands.length
          ? 'the whole vocabulary can win, tail included'
          : 'the dart only sees what is left, renormalised',
      x0,
      SIDE.y + 56,
      12,
      inkA(0.55)
    );

    const by = SIDE.y + 96;
    text('probability kept by the cut', x0, by - 10, 11, inkA(0.5), 'left', true);
    ctx.fillStyle = inkA(0.12);
    ctx.fillRect(x0, by, maxW, 22);
    ctx.fillStyle = hexA(KEEP, 0.8);
    ctx.fillRect(x0, by, Math.max(2, keptMass * maxW), 22);
    text(`${(keptMass * 100).toFixed(1)}%`, x0 + 8, by + 16, 12, inkA(0.95), 'left', true);
    if (keptMass < 0.999)
      text(`${((1 - keptMass) * 100).toFixed(1)}% thrown away`, x0 + maxW, by + 38, 11, inkA(0.45), 'right', true);

    const seen = cands.filter((c) => c.n > 0).length;
    const rows: [string, string][] = [
      ['words in the vocabulary', String(cands.length)],
      ['seen after this context', String(seen)],
      ['given a share anyway', String(cands.length - seen)],
      ['kept by the cut', `${keptN} of ${cands.length}`],
      [
        'last pick',
        shot
          ? `${shot.word}  ${(shot.prob * 100).toFixed(1)}%  ${(-Math.log2(Math.max(1e-9, shot.base))).toFixed(1)} bits`
          : 'nothing yet',
      ],
    ];
    rows.forEach(([k, v], i) => {
      const y = SIDE.y + 190 + i * 25;
      text(k, x0, y, 11, inkA(0.5), 'left', true);
      text(v, x0 + maxW, y, 12, i === 4 && shot ? CHOSEN : inkA(0.9), 'right', true);
    });
  }

  // --- 4. the dart ----------------------------------------------------------------

  function drawDart() {
    panel(DARTP, 'THE DART THAT PICKED THE LAST WORD');
    if (!shot) {
      text(
        'press Next word (or the s key) and watch where the dart lands',
        DARTP.x + DARTP.w / 2,
        DARTP.y + 54,
        13,
        inkA(0.4),
        'center'
      );
      return;
    }
    text(`"${shot.ctxStr}"  →  "${shot.word}"`, DARTP.x + 18, DARTP.y + 26, 12, inkA(0.6), 'left', true);
    if (shot.cutCount)
      text(
        `${shot.kept.length} words on the strip, ${shot.cutCount} cut before the throw`,
        DARTP.x + DARTP.w - 18,
        DARTP.y + 26,
        11,
        inkA(0.42),
        'right',
        true
      );

    const sx = DARTP.x + 30, sw = DARTP.w - 60, sy = DARTP.y + 44, sh = 26;
    let acc = 0;
    shot.kept.forEach((seg, i) => {
      const w = seg.p * sw;
      const win = seg.w === shot!.word;
      ctx.fillStyle = win ? CHOSEN : hexA(KEEP, i % 2 ? 0.4 : 0.62);
      ctx.fillRect(sx + acc, sy, Math.max(0.6, w), sh);
      if (w > 44) text(seg.w, sx + acc + w / 2, sy + 17, 11, win ? '#0d0e12' : inkA(0.95), 'center');
      acc += w;
    });
    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.18);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.strokeRect(sx, sy, sw, sh);
    text('0', sx - 6, sy + 17, 10, inkA(0.4), 'right', true);
    text('1', sx + sw + 6, sy + 17, 10, inkA(0.4), 'left', true);

    if (shot.r >= 0) {
      const dx = sx + shot.r * sw;
      ctx.strokeStyle = DART;
      ctx.lineWidth = 2;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(dx, sy - 9);
      ctx.lineTo(dx, sy + sh + 6);
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.fillStyle = DART;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(dx, sy - 2);
      ctx.lineTo(dx - 5, sy - 11);
      ctx.lineTo(dx + 5, sy - 11);
      ctx.closePath();
      ctx.fill();
      text(
        `random number ${shot.r.toFixed(3)}`,
        dx,
        sy + sh + 18,
        11,
        DART,
        dx > sx + sw / 2 ? 'right' : 'left',
        true
      );
    } else {
      text('greedy throws no dart', sx + sw / 2, sy + sh + 18, 11, inkA(0.45), 'center', true);
    }
  }

  // --- 5. the whole vocabulary -----------------------------------------------------

  function drawVocab(cands: Cand[]) {
    panel(VOC, `THE WHOLE VOCABULARY: ALL ${V} WORDS, EVERY ONE WITH A PROBABILITY`);
    const byWord = new Map(cands.map((c) => [c.w, c]));
    let maxBase = 0;
    for (const c of cands) maxBase = Math.max(maxBase, c.base);

    const x0 = VOC.x + 16, areaW = VOC.w - 32, areaH = VOC.h - 48;
    const cols = Math.max(1, Math.floor(areaW / 132));
    const rows = Math.ceil(V / cols);
    const gap = 3;
    const cw = areaW / cols;
    const chh = Math.min(26, Math.floor((areaH - (rows - 1) * gap) / rows));
    const y0 = VOC.y + 28;

    VOCAB.forEach((w, i) => {
      const c = byWord.get(w)!;
      const cx = x0 + (i % cols) * cw;
      const cy = y0 + Math.floor(i / cols) * (chh + gap);
      const cellW = cw - 8;
      const frac = c.base / Math.max(1e-9, maxBase);
      // the cell is the bar: it fills from the left in proportion to the word's
      // own probability, so the whole vocabulary reads as one chart
      const ty = cy + chh / 2 + 4;
      ctx.fillStyle = inkA(0.07);
      rr(cx, cy, cellW, chh, 5);
      ctx.fill();
      ctx.fillStyle = hexA(c.kept ? KEEP : CUTC, c.kept ? 0.5 : 0.3);
      rr(cx, cy, Math.max(3, cellW * frac), chh, 5);
      ctx.fill();
      if (c.kept) {
        ctx.strokeStyle = hexA(KEEP, 0.75);
        ctx.lineWidth = 1;
        rr(cx, cy, cellW, chh, 5);
        ctx.stroke();
      }
      if (flash > 0 && shot && shot.word === w) {
        ctx.fillStyle = hexA(CHOSEN, 0.45 * flash);
        rr(cx, cy, cellW, chh, 5);
        ctx.fill();
      }
      text(w, cx + 8, ty, 12, inkA(c.kept ? 0.98 : 0.6));
      text(
        `${(c.base * 100).toFixed(c.base < 0.01 ? 2 : 0)}%`,
        cx + cellW - 8,
        ty,
        10,
        inkA(0.45),
        'right',
        true
      );
    });

    text(
      'filled part = its probability · blue = kept by the cut · red = in the tail that was thrown away',
      VOC.x + 16,
      VOC.y + VOC.h - 12,
      10,
      inkA(0.4),
      'left',
      true
    );
  }

  // --- readouts ---------------------------------------------------------------------

  const el = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id) as HTMLElement;
  const setEq = equationBar();

  function updateHud(cands: Cand[]) {
    const keptN = cands.filter((c) => c.kept).length;
    const keptMass = cands.reduce((s, c) => s + (c.kept ? c.q : 0), 0);
    el('vocab').textContent = String(V);
    el('seen').textContent = String(cands.filter((c) => c.n > 0).length);
    el('kept').textContent = `${keptN} of ${V}`;
    el('mass').textContent = `${(keptMass * 100).toFixed(1)}%`;
    el('pick').textContent = shot ? `${shot.word} (${(shot.prob * 100).toFixed(1)}%)` : '—';
    el('bits').textContent = shot ? `${(-Math.log2(Math.max(1e-9, shot.base))).toFixed(2)} bits` : '—';

    setEq([
      ['x_{t+1}\\sim P(\\,\\cdot\\mid x_1\\dots x_t)'],
      [
        [`T = ${state.temp.toFixed(2)}`, DART],
        [`\\quad k = ${state.greedy ? 1 : state.k}`, KEEP],
        [`\\quad p = ${state.p.toFixed(2)}`, KEEP],
        [`\\quad |S| = ${keptN}\\ \\text{of}\\ ${V}`, KEEP],
      ],
      ['score every word, reshape with temperature, cut the tail, throw a dart'],
    ]);
  }

  // --- loop ------------------------------------------------------------------------

  function draw() {
    ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);
    ctx.textBaseline = 'alphabetic';
    const cands = candidates();
    drawText();
    drawDist(cands);
    drawSide(cands);
    drawDart();
    drawVocab(cands);
    updateHud(cands);
  }

  let acc = 0, last = 0;
  function loop(ts: number) {
    if (!last) last = ts;
    const dt = Math.min(0.05, (ts - last) / 1000);
    last = ts;
    if (state.running) {
      acc += dt * state.speed;
      while (acc >= 1) { acc -= 1; stepOnce(); }
    }
    if (flash > 0) flash = Math.max(0, flash - dt * 1.6);
    draw();
    requestAnimationFrame(loop);
  }

  // --- controls ----------------------------------------------------------------------

  const wrapEl = el('wrap');
  function setGreedy(g: boolean) {
    state.greedy = g;
    wrapEl.className = g ? 'sim greedy' : 'sim';
    document
      .querySelectorAll('#mode button')
      .forEach((b) =>
        b.classList.toggle('active', ((b as HTMLElement).dataset.m === 'greedy') === g)
      );
  }
  el('mode').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    const btn = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('button');
    if (btn) setGreedy(btn.dataset.m === 'greedy');
  });

  const bind = (id: string, f: (v: number) => void, fmt: (v: number) => string) => {
    const inp = el(id) as HTMLInputElement;
    const apply = () => {
      f(+inp.value);
      el(id + 'val').textContent = fmt(+inp.value);
    };
    inp.addEventListener('input', apply);
    apply();
  };
  (el('k') as HTMLInputElement).max = String(V);
  (el('k') as HTMLInputElement).value = String(V);
  bind('n', (v) => (state.n = v), String);
  bind('t', (v) => (state.temp = v / 100), (v) => (v / 100).toFixed(2));
  bind('k', (v) => (state.k = v), (v) => (v >= V ? 'off' : v === 1 ? '1 (greedy)' : String(v)));
  bind('p', (v) => (state.p = v / 100), (v) => (v >= 100 ? 'off' : (v / 100).toFixed(2)));
  bind('sp', (v) => (state.speed = v), String);

  const runBtn = el('run') as HTMLButtonElement;
  runBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    state.running = !state.running;
    runBtn.textContent = state.running ? 'Pause' : 'Run';
  });
  el('step').addEventListener('click', () => stepOnce());
  el('reset').addEventListener('click', () => seed());

  buildModels();
  setGreedy(false);
  seed();
  requestAnimationFrame(loop);
</script>

<style>
  /* the three knobs only matter when there is a dart to aim */
  .greedy .tunes {
    opacity: 0.4;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
</style>
